>> title: Chicken Tikka, Air Fryer
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, indian, air fryer, basket, yogurt, starter
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: chicken-tikka
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer chicken tikka, murgh tikka, basket tikka, tandoori chicken in the air fryer
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the yoghurt sets into a crust two minutes before the thigh is done, and past that the crust darkens while the meat dries
>> washing-up: the marinating bowl, the basket
>> capacity: 4 — one 5.7 L air fryer basket, roast, air fry
>> keeps: 3 days — the crust softens but the marinade has done its work; better cold in bread than warmed twice

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. Thick yoghurt clings in the draught; a pourable batter would blow off.
No skewers. The pieces sit straight on the basket, which is why this is two things.

>> step: marinate 20 min in the bowl, no skewers
Marinate @boneless chicken thighs{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; in 2-in pieces, slashed) in a #bowl{} with @whole-milk yogurt{1/2%cup}(120 g), @lemon juice{1%Tbs}, @ginger-garlic paste{1%Tbs}, @garam masala{1%tsp}, @Kashmiri chile powder{2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} for ~marinate{20%min}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 12–15 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)marinated chicken{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{13%min}, one layer and not touching.

>> step: turn at seven minutes — crust set and freckled, 74°C inside
Turn @&(~1)tikka{} once.

>> step: scatter the onion and cilantro at the table
Scatter @red onion{1/2}(sliced thin), @cilantro{2%Tbs}(picked) over @&(~1)tikka{} with @lemon{1%wedge}.

>> step: Twenty minutes takes the salt and the spice in. Six hours is better, and the plain file is where to go for it.
The shelf's promise is a 45-minute clock, so the marinade is inside it.
